Scrolls, !water, spells, and some other things take effect on the whole
stack, not just one item.

IIRC, I had 5 seprate stacks of daggers (blessed +2, blessed +1,
uncursed +1, uncursed +0, cursed +0), 2 extra potions of holy water,
some markers and enough blank paper to write as many blessed/uncursed
?enchant weapon as necessary.

I used 2 *uncursed* scrolls of enchant weapon and 2 potions of holy
water to make all 42 daggers into one big stack of 42 blessed +2
daggers.  After that, making them blessed rustproof +7 daggers was
rather easy.

Collecting that many daggers was harder than enchanting them.  I had to
sort through piles and piles of bodies while taking the scenic tour of
the Gnomish Mines.  Don't those pesky gnomes and dwarves ever learn ...
never mess with an elf on holiday. :-)

There are more resource efficient ways of doing this (namely, cancel
all the stacks and start from the beginning with a whole boatload of
uncursed +0 daggers), but I didn't have a /cancellation handy.

